WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.481 --> 00:00:03.517
(dulcet music)

00:00:03.517 --> 00:00:07.050
(audience cheers)

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:08.730
- [Andrew] Josh is a dancer.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:09.563
- [Josh] I'm.

00:00:09.563 --> 00:00:10.396
- [Kelly] Dancing feels good.

00:00:10.396 --> 00:00:12.805
- Dancing feels so nice.
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:00:12.805 --> 00:00:14.859
- [Andrew] We're here in person with you.

00:00:14.859 --> 00:00:15.692
- I know.

00:00:15.692 --> 00:00:16.525
- And welcome to New York.

00:00:16.525 --> 00:00:17.610
- Yes.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:18.443
- Thank you.

00:00:18.443 --> 00:00:19.276
- How do you like it?

00:00:19.276 --> 00:00:20.550
- [Kelly] I love it. My
hands are cold, I'm sorry.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:21.660
- Well, 'cause you're in New York, now.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:22.493
- [Kelly] It is, I know.

00:00:22.493 --> 00:00:23.603
- It's cold in New York.

00:00:23.603 --> 00:00:25.552
- I love it though. The
layering, the fall weather.

00:00:25.552 --> 00:00:26.389
- [Andrew] Yeah, it's beautiful.

00:00:26.389 --> 00:00:27.222
- [Josh] It's a good time of year.

00:00:27.222 --> 00:00:29.580
- Yeah, I'm so excited
to have you both here.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:30.413
- [Andrew] Thank you.

00:00:30.413 --> 00:00:32.610
- I'm excited you're having us here.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.123
Andrew didn't wanna do it.
And I was like, we have to.

00:00:35.123 --> 00:00:37.026
(all laugh)

00:00:37.026 --> 00:00:39.200
- I pissed him off in the Zoom.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.710
(Andrew and Josh laugh)

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:43.260
So like, who chose to do the
kid photos on the Playbill.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:44.370
I love that.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:46.020
- We, did it together.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.730
- [Andrew] We did it together,
'cause we were talking.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.950
- [Kelly] Because the whole
thing is about dreams, right?

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:51.285
It's about, yeah. Dreams.

00:00:51.285 --> 00:00:52.883
- [Andrew] Can you guys
guess which one is which?

00:00:52.883 --> 00:00:54.090
(audience laughs)

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:56.250
Well no, we were talking about
the, you know, first of all,

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.170
we were asked to pick
headshots for the playbill,

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.430
which I don't know about you,
but I hate picking pictures.

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:01.630
- Oh my gosh. I got in
the wrong line of work.

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:02.715
I hate photos.

00:01:02.715 --> 00:01:03.548
- Yeah. It's just, I'm like-

00:01:03.548 --> 00:01:04.980
So then we were talking about it.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:07.470
And I was like, we
should use kid pictures.

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:09.660
Because it is about two
guys who have this dream

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:10.493
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:10.493 --> 00:01:11.326
- Of taking a show to Broadway.

00:01:11.326 --> 00:01:14.460
And that's around the age that
we both sort of discovered

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.092
that that's what we wanted to do.

00:01:16.092 --> 00:01:16.925
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:16.925 --> 00:01:18.876
- We wanted to be actors, and
we wanted to be on Broadway.

00:01:18.876 --> 00:01:19.709
- [Kelly] You got the bug.
- Yeah.

00:01:19.709 --> 00:01:21.958
So we chose those photos.

00:01:21.958 --> 00:01:23.160
- I love instead that.
- [Josh] To be fair,

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:24.840
we did those pictures as kids, knowing

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.880
that one day they would
be used as headshots

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.438
for Gutenberg, the Musical.

00:01:28.438 --> 00:01:29.271
- [Kelly] Exactly.

00:01:29.271 --> 00:01:30.104
- So it was very forward thinking.

00:01:30.104 --> 00:01:30.937
- [Andrew] We really thought ahead.

00:01:30.937 --> 00:01:32.103
We're long planners.

00:01:32.103 --> 00:01:32.936
- We're planners.

00:01:32.936 --> 00:01:33.769
- I know, I like that about y'all.

00:01:33.769 --> 00:01:36.420
So what you knew, like what hit you?

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.910
Like, what did you see, that
you knew you wanted to be

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:41.370
in musical theater, or in
entertainment in general?

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:45.300
- Oh man, you know, I saw Peter Pan,

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:49.500
with Kathy Rigby, when I was
about five years old, on tour.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.770
And I said one day, I'm not
gonna be able to play that part.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.241
But I'd like to play something else.

00:01:54.241 --> 00:01:56.190
(audience laughs)

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:57.750
- Very self-aware, at a young age.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.583
- [Andrew] Yeah, you knew what

00:01:58.583 --> 00:01:59.416
your limitations were.

00:01:59.416 --> 00:02:00.383
- Yeah.
- Well, it took me a second

00:02:00.383 --> 00:02:03.090
to find musical theater.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:06.990
But what I wanted to be first,
was a Solid Gold dancer.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:08.130
- [Kelly] A Solid Gold dancer?

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:10.027
- Yes. Does anyone remember Solid Gold?

00:02:10.027 --> 00:02:11.377
(Josh laughs)

00:02:11.377 --> 00:02:13.107
- Oh, I was like, that was very specific.

00:02:13.107 --> 00:02:15.900
- It was a variety show, they had dancers.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:17.970
I wanted to do that. And then I realized

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.910
that there's actually a
different job, called an actor.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:21.743
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:21.743 --> 00:02:22.576
- Where you could do musicals.

00:02:22.576 --> 00:02:24.030
And I started watching the Tony Awards.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:25.252
And then that really,

00:02:25.252 --> 00:02:26.820
- I got in trouble as a kid.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:28.890
'Cause I was a big
performer, even as a child.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:31.950
So my mom got called
to the school one day.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:34.050
Because, as a kindergartner,

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.900
I would apparently walk into class late.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.000
What kindergartner walks in late.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.200
- So this all tracks.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.033
- This all tracks.

00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:42.930
And I would, apparently open the door,

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:45.329
look at my teacher and go, "Hiya Toots."

00:02:45.329 --> 00:02:48.540
And they called my mom to the school.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:53.540
Or I would say, "Hiya
Toots" or "Lucy, I'm home!"

00:02:53.892 --> 00:02:56.340
- It was apparently not okay.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.350
- You were a born performer.
- I was a born performer.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:02:59.910
- That's amazing. You're
reminding me of my son.

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:00.743
That is so my son, Remy, because-

00:03:00.743 --> 00:03:03.291
- He's got a very horrible future.

00:03:03.291 --> 00:03:04.800
(Josh laughs)

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.780
- No, he's that kind
of entertaining though.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.820
He's a sponge. He watches
something , he loves it.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.740
He just, it comes, he regurgitates it.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:12.060
Yeah, it's awesome.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:12.893
- [Josh] It's a curse.

00:03:12.893 --> 00:03:13.726
- So wait, so Halloween.

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:16.070
It's not a curse, it's a
blessing. It's a blessing.

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:18.598
It's a 'blurse'. It's both.

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:20.520
So Halloween is coming up.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:23.130
I know you got kiddos. So, what do y'all-

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:24.030
Do you dress up?

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:25.260
'Cause I know that we had the cute

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:26.100
little photos of your children.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.630
But I also found this one of you.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:30.151
And I just have a quick
question here, Andrew.

00:03:30.151 --> 00:03:31.890
(all laugh)

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:35.130
Like what, I don't know,
that I've ever known a kid

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:36.697
that dresses as the Pope.

00:03:36.697 --> 00:03:37.800
- The Pope, yeah.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.330
- You're a very serious kid.

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:41.635
- [Andrew] It was a very Catholic idea.

00:03:41.635 --> 00:03:42.520
- [Kelly] Very serious.

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:43.353
- My brother and his family are here,

00:03:43.353 --> 00:03:45.372
so he was witness to this.

00:03:45.372 --> 00:03:46.307
- What's up?

00:03:46.307 --> 00:03:47.457
- Rannells family.

00:03:47.457 --> 00:03:48.360
- Hi.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:52.080
- [Andrew] So yeah, my grandma
Josephine, had this idea

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.910
that I was gonna be the Pope.

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:55.860
So she put together that costume.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.330
She got me, and I was the Pope.

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:59.920
And my little sister,
Natalie, was an angel.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:02.970
But it's still like, hands down, I'm 45.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:04.290
That's my best Halloween costume.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:05.220
- [Kelly] Oh my God, I love you.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.110
- It's the pope, it
peaked at Fourth grade.

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:08.100
- Can you imagine trick or treat?

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.537
I've just never seen a
kid dressed as a Pope.

00:04:09.537 --> 00:04:11.400
- As the Pope. I was very popular.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:12.875
- [Kelly] It's especially like Tony Stark.

00:04:12.875 --> 00:04:14.316
(Josh laughs)

00:04:14.316 --> 00:04:16.020
- I was very popular, people
took a lot of pictures of me.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:17.070
It was like, yeah, I felt-

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:17.910
- [Kelly] You were a hit.

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:18.743
- I was a hit.

00:04:18.743 --> 00:04:20.710
- [Kelly] Okay, well I have
to pull this one up, too.

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:21.543
- Oh,

00:04:21.543 --> 00:04:22.446
- [Andrew] Josh, please.

00:04:22.446 --> 00:04:23.700
- This was last year,
and this was incredible.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.119
- [Josh] Yes.

00:04:25.119 --> 00:04:26.409
- [Kelly] This is incredible.

00:04:26.409 --> 00:04:27.505
(audience cheers)

00:04:27.505 --> 00:04:28.553
- [Josh] I mean,

00:04:28.553 --> 00:04:29.841
- [Kelly] Flotsam and jetsam.

00:04:29.841 --> 00:04:32.067
- What's really complicated,

00:04:32.067 --> 00:04:34.350
what's really complicated
about this picture is,

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:36.313
I was also trying to be the Pope.

00:04:36.313 --> 00:04:37.561
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:37.561 --> 00:04:38.394
- [Josh] It is tricky.

00:04:38.394 --> 00:04:39.227
- They're layers.

00:04:39.227 --> 00:04:40.440
- Something went very wrong.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:41.550
- [Andrew] Someone led you astray, Joshua.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:44.310
- No, I lost a bet with my
daughters. I lost a bet.

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:45.960
They said if you lose this bet,

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:48.180
you have to be Ursula, for Halloween.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:51.090
And so I ended up being
Ursula for Halloween.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.290
- [Kelly] Please tell me you walked around

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:53.123
trick-or-treating with them,

00:04:53.123 --> 00:04:54.507
singing 'Poor unfortunate Souls'.

00:04:54.507 --> 00:04:55.675
- [Josh] Oh, a hundred percent.

00:04:55.675 --> 00:04:56.508
- Okay.

00:04:56.508 --> 00:04:57.961
You would've let me down.

00:04:57.961 --> 00:04:58.794
- Oh yeah.

00:04:58.794 --> 00:04:59.627
- Do you like to dress up?

00:04:59.627 --> 00:05:01.201
- I love to dress up.

00:05:01.201 --> 00:05:02.034
- Right.

00:05:02.034 --> 00:05:03.150
- I love a theme. I don't
even wanna go to a party

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.080
unless it's themed.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:05.103
- [Andrew] Yeah.

00:05:05.103 --> 00:05:06.899
- Like why, you're just gonna
hang out, and be yourself.

00:05:06.899 --> 00:05:07.732
That's boring.

00:05:07.732 --> 00:05:09.054
- [Andrew] You don't
like to go to any parties

00:05:09.054 --> 00:05:10.374
unless you're themed, or just Halloween?

00:05:10.374 --> 00:05:11.207
I'm gonna, let's be real.

00:05:11.207 --> 00:05:13.140
- I'm sorry, I can't attend your wedding

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:15.750
unless everybody's
dressed up as a character.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.240
- Wait, I did throw a themed
party, one time though.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:20.400
And Enrique Iglesias showed up and-

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:21.233
- [Andrew] No,
- Because we had the same

00:05:21.233 --> 00:05:22.066
manager at the time.

00:05:22.066 --> 00:05:24.313
I don't hang out with
famous people, I'm not cool.

00:05:24.313 --> 00:05:26.940
But he showed up, and
he wasn't in costume.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:29.970
And at that point I'd had a lot to drink.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:32.547
And so I was very bold, and walked up

00:05:32.547 --> 00:05:35.019
and was like, get out,
you don't have a costume.

00:05:35.019 --> 00:05:36.502
(Josh laughs)

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.520
- I was like, you have to
wear a costume to be here.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:39.840
And I was like, I'm just kidding.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:41.640
But kind of get out. I'm sorry.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:42.840
- Also, get a costume.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.031
- [Josh] Yeah.

00:05:44.031 --> 00:05:46.020
- [Kelly] I can't rap. It
says rap, and there's nothing.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:47.446
But I will make (beep) up.

00:05:47.446 --> 00:05:48.550
- [Andrew] There's nothing to rap.

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:49.891
- Okay, I was like, it says rap.

00:05:49.891 --> 00:05:52.209
And I was like, I dunno if you've noticed-

00:05:52.209 --> 00:05:54.291
- You can rap.

00:05:54.291 --> 00:05:56.345
You can totally rap.
- [Kelly] I can not rap.

00:05:56.345 --> 00:05:58.681
- Hi, we'll be back after this break.

00:05:58.681 --> 00:06:00.619
(all laugh)

00:06:00.619 --> 00:06:03.000
- So I'm not just saying this.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.800
I've literally heard so
much, 'cause everybody here

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.240
also talks about shows, right.

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.230
Nonstop, which I love.

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:09.090
But everybody is talking
about Gutenberg, the musical.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:09.923
So where did this come from?

00:06:09.923 --> 00:06:10.756
- [Josh] That's your show.

00:06:10.756 --> 00:06:12.540
- [Andrew] You're in it too, look Josh.

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:13.373
- [Josh] That's us.

00:06:13.373 --> 00:06:14.206
- [Andrew] That's us.

00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:16.260
- You are about, two men
in one dream. No chance.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:17.250
I like it.

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:18.330
Says it all, right there.

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:19.620
- [Josh] That's it, that's
all you need to know.

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:22.230
- So what do people
need to know, coming in?

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:23.063
- Hmm.

00:06:23.063 --> 00:06:24.158
- [Kelly] Or do you want them to know?

00:06:24.158 --> 00:06:27.330
- Well, we're in it. Well
no, so it's about two guys,

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:28.740
named Bud and Doug.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.960
Who have decided, they're sort of new fans

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:31.800
of musical theater.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:33.810
They wanna write a musical,

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:35.520
they wanna write a hit musical.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:38.010
So they decide that a historical musical,

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:39.270
- [Josh] Can I just say,
you're doing great right now.

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:40.560
- Thank you very much.

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:41.820
A historical musical.

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:42.870
Those do well.

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:43.855
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:43.855 --> 00:06:46.170
So they pick, to write a
musical about Johann Gutenberg,

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:48.270
the inventor of the printing press.

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:50.376
'Cause isn't that like a fun, sexy idea?

00:06:50.376 --> 00:06:51.300
(audience laughs)

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:52.860
- I have a quicker pitch, which is,

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:54.660
it's the Hamilton of our generation.

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:55.720
- No.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:57.750
(audience laughs and applauds)

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:00.540
- I've explained this to Josh, many times.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.790
Hamilton, is the Hamilton
of our generation.

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:03.750
- Hamilton.

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:05.790
- It's the other Hamilton
of our generation.

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:07.118
- [Kelly] It's the other one.

00:07:07.118 --> 00:07:09.420
- No, we're having the best time.

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:10.253
- Yes.

00:07:10.253 --> 00:07:12.030
- Rannells and I, the last
time I was on Broadway

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:13.860
was over a decade ago.

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:16.440
I've been, when we did
Book of Mormon together.

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:18.336
And I've been wanting to come back.

00:07:18.336 --> 00:07:19.169
(audience applauds)

00:07:19.169 --> 00:07:20.002
Thank you so much.

00:07:20.002 --> 00:07:20.835
- [Kelly] So good.

00:07:20.835 --> 00:07:21.840
- And I've been wanting to come back,

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:24.540
and I only really wanted
to come back with him.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:26.490
'Cause he's the only person
who would perform with me.

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:27.693
- [Andrew] Well, work with you.

00:07:27.693 --> 00:07:28.526
- And so,

00:07:28.526 --> 00:07:30.120
- And finally the
restraining orders ran out.

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:31.615
- Yeah, they lifted it.
- [Andrew] So then I was able

00:07:31.615 --> 00:07:32.930
to get back on stage.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:35.400
- So physically, we could
work together again.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:36.498
- Legally,

00:07:36.498 --> 00:07:37.500
- But it's been, you know,

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:39.438
the world needs some laughter right now.

00:07:39.438 --> 00:07:42.480
It's a sad time in the world.

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:45.300
And it's been really refreshing to be able

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:47.190
to provide people with that sense

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:50.310
of just, two hours of escapism.

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:51.540
And we get to be idiots.

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:54.480
And we play, each of us
plays about 20 characters.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:57.683
We have 150 hats, that
we wear in this show.

00:07:57.683 --> 00:07:59.816
- Literal hats.
- Literal hats.

00:07:59.816 --> 00:08:02.400
- I hear that it's chaos
backstage, is this true?

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:03.233
I can imagine.

00:08:03.233 --> 00:08:04.290
- [Josh] Yes, it is chaos.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:05.190
- This is a strange show,

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:07.230
because we're on stage the entire time.

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:08.207
Like, once Josh and I go out there.

00:08:08.207 --> 00:08:09.960
- Oh, so there's no break.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.730
What if you have to pee?

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:12.563
- We do it on stage.

00:08:12.563 --> 00:08:14.040
- [Andrew] Well, there's an interval.

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:14.873
- Okay.

00:08:14.873 --> 00:08:16.350
- [Andrew] Josh, where's
the diaper? Well actually,

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:18.673
- By the way, I wear a
man diaper in the show.

00:08:18.673 --> 00:08:21.240
- Would you like to explain this?

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:23.640
- [Josh] I wanna tell you
guys, when we first started

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:27.030
doing the show, I had my shirt tucked in.

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:28.700
And every time I danced, it would come up.

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:29.533
- It would come up.

00:08:29.533 --> 00:08:32.303
- And you would just
see too much of my body.

00:08:32.303 --> 00:08:33.259
(audience laugh)

00:08:33.259 --> 00:08:36.210
And so, they said to me,
we have to button you

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:37.627
into your pants.

00:08:37.627 --> 00:08:38.460
(audience laughs)

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:41.640
- Now, the technical term
for this, is a crotch strap.

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:42.920
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:46.667
- But the untechnical term
for it, is a pain in the ass.

00:08:46.667 --> 00:08:47.500
- Okay.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.860
- 'Cause I have to
basically wear this diaper

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:51.150
that I'm fastened into.

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:52.297
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:08:52.297 --> 00:08:53.370
- [Andrew] So, he's wearing a onesie.

00:08:53.370 --> 00:08:55.350
- And sometimes, you know, before a show

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:57.120
you need to go number two, or four.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:57.953
- Joshua.

00:08:57.953 --> 00:08:58.786
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:08:58.786 --> 00:08:59.619
- [Josh] We all get it, it's okay.

00:08:59.619 --> 00:09:00.452
- You wanna feel lighter?

00:09:00.452 --> 00:09:01.468
- [Josh] This is a safe space.

00:09:01.468 --> 00:09:02.984
- Yeah, I feel comfortable.

00:09:02.984 --> 00:09:04.440
(audience applauds)

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:08.010
- In order to do what I
need to do, as a human,

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:11.790
I have to have a grown
man, unbuttoned 20 buttons.

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:13.380
- I don't help with this.

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:15.180
- No, but Andrew watches.

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:17.124
- I do watch it, like this.

00:09:17.124 --> 00:09:18.180
(Kelly laughs)

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:19.013
- I watch like that.

00:09:19.013 --> 00:09:20.460
- So wait, have you had a moment?

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:21.750
'Cause I've had moments on tour,

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:24.780
where I'm on stage, and I'm like,

00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:26.250
- I had a moment during Book of Mormon

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:28.260
where I felt my stomach drop.

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:29.093
- [Kelly] Oh no.

00:09:29.093 --> 00:09:30.189
- And I was like,

00:09:30.189 --> 00:09:31.579
- And the sweat, the one bead of sweat.

00:09:31.579 --> 00:09:34.038
- Oh, the sweat started coming,
and the audience was like,

00:09:34.038 --> 00:09:35.774
why does that character
look so uncomfortable?

00:09:35.774 --> 00:09:36.854
(audience laughs)

00:09:36.854 --> 00:09:37.898
- [Andrew] You made it through.

00:09:37.898 --> 00:09:38.910
- Well, I literally
remember, I was timing.

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:40.710
I had a minute and a half.

00:09:40.710 --> 00:09:43.080
There was a bathroom
right next to- this is not

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:43.913
where I wanted this to go.

00:09:43.913 --> 00:09:45.510
- [Andrew] No, this has
really taking a turn.

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:47.550
- [Kelly] I'm just
saying, you were already

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:48.383
wearing a diaper.

00:09:48.383 --> 00:09:51.024
- This is my fault, and I
apologize to everyone watching.

00:09:51.024 --> 00:09:53.046
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:09:53.046 --> 00:09:54.000
- We'll just, but the diaper is part

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.920
of the glamour of Broadway.

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:57.030
- [Josh] Yeah.

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:58.683
- You've been friends for so long now.

00:09:58.683 --> 00:10:01.350
(audience laughs)

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:03.390
You tolerate each other,
you've tolerated each other

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:04.223
for at least a decade.

00:10:04.223 --> 00:10:05.056
- [Andrew] Sure, sure.

00:10:05.056 --> 00:10:07.230
- So wait, are there times, because it is

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:09.660
a hard industry, and I think
everybody always thinks

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:12.120
we're all barbecuing
together, all the time.

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:13.590
But sometimes you don't, like I don't have

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:14.423
a lot of friends that are like,

00:10:14.423 --> 00:10:16.348
- No, sometimes we saute together.

00:10:16.348 --> 00:10:19.142
- [Kelly] So wait, do you
have those times though?

00:10:19.142 --> 00:10:20.820
It seems like that kind of friendship

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:22.800
that you can connect, when
you're like, man, this is hard.

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:23.910
Like when you're being serious.

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:24.930
- Well, we went, you know,

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:26.280
doing the Book of Mormon together.

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:29.070
Obviously we could not
have predicted that show

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:30.990
would've been as successful as it was.

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:31.823
- [Kelly] Really?

00:10:31.823 --> 00:10:32.656
- Yeah, I mean,

00:10:32.656 --> 00:10:34.217
- I thought it was gonna
close within three weeks.

00:10:34.217 --> 00:10:35.280
- Yeah, we were sort of
all nervous about it.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:36.779
- Wow, you have no pulse on the people.

00:10:36.779 --> 00:10:39.330
- [Josh] By the way, I thought Frozen

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:40.290
was gonna be a bomb, too.

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:41.592
I was like, what do I know.

00:10:41.592 --> 00:10:44.640
- Josh, you really, yeah,
you've got your finger

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:45.630
on the pulse.

00:10:45.630 --> 00:10:47.640
But we got to go through that
whole experience together.

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:49.080
We went through the Tony Awards together.

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:51.120
We both moved back to
Los Angeles together.

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:52.800
We both had TV shows together.

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:54.304
They both got canceled together.

00:10:54.304 --> 00:10:55.328
(Josh laughs)

00:10:55.328 --> 00:10:56.670
We gotta go through all of it.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:58.923
- [Kelly] Best of friends.
You do everything together.

00:10:58.923 --> 00:11:01.620
- And you know, I could
look at Josh, and be like,

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:04.248
oh, you know exactly what I
am going through right now.

00:11:04.248 --> 00:11:05.539
- Which is hard to describe to people.

00:11:05.539 --> 00:11:06.372
- Which is very rare.

00:11:06.372 --> 00:11:07.205
- Yeah, it is.

00:11:07.205 --> 00:11:09.163
And we really- now, you know,

00:11:09.163 --> 00:11:11.880
over a decade into this relationship,

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:14.460
we know when the other person needs space

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:16.680
from everybody encroaching on us.

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:17.634
So it's like,

00:11:17.634 --> 00:11:19.019
- Sometimes I need a snack.

00:11:19.019 --> 00:11:20.100
- Sometimes he needs,
sometimes he gets hangry.

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:21.609
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:11:21.609 --> 00:11:22.500
- And I'm like, Vesuvius
is about to burst.

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:25.680
I need to protect the citizens of Pompeii.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:27.990
I need to protect all the
citizens of Pompeii right now.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:29.015
- Yeah.

00:11:29.015 --> 00:11:29.848
- Give Andrew five minutes.

00:11:29.848 --> 00:11:30.681
- He needs a cracker.

00:11:30.681 --> 00:11:31.590
- He needs a cracker.

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:32.910
- Yes, Shelby needs his juice.

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:34.940
- But vice versa, we both sort of,

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:35.850
- We know.

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:39.060
- We protect each other,
in a way that only comes

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:41.357
with time, and barbecuing together.

00:11:41.357 --> 00:11:42.330
(audience laughs)

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:43.163
- [Andrew] We need to do that.

00:11:43.163 --> 00:11:43.996
- We've never done that.

00:11:43.996 --> 00:11:44.829
- We need to do that.

00:11:44.829 --> 00:11:46.217
- [Kelly] Oh, look at this.
Moments are being made.

00:11:46.217 --> 00:11:47.494
- Three of us, are gonna barbecue.

00:11:47.494 --> 00:11:49.710
- [Kelly] I love barbecue.
Don't invite me. Yeah,

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:50.850
- [Josh] We're gonna do it.

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:52.623
- [Andrew] It'll be a themed barbecue

00:11:52.623 --> 00:11:54.640
- Themed, I won't show up, unless a theme.

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:56.130
- We'll have a theme party.

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:56.963
- Yeah.

00:11:56.963 --> 00:11:57.930
- We'll come back for a cooking segment.

00:11:57.930 --> 00:11:59.467
- We all have to dress up
like toy story characters.

00:11:59.467 --> 00:12:00.921
(Andrew and Josh laugh)

